Package: shield-packet-collector
Version: VERSION_PLACEHOLDER
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Zuken Shield Contributors
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-scapy, libcap2-bin
Suggests: shield-monitor
Description: Optional packet-capture helper for Zuken Shield
 Observes ARP, DHCP, ICMP, NDP, TCP handshake and outbound DNS packets and
 publishes structured observations to Zuken Shield over a local Unix socket.
 .
 This is a SEPARATE component from the Shield core on purpose. It depends on
 scapy, which is distributed under the GPL-2.0, while the Shield core targets
 the Apache-2.0 licence. Running the two as distinct programs in distinct
 processes keeps that boundary explicit and testable. This packaging choice is
 an architectural one; it is not, and does not claim to be, a legal conclusion.
 .
 Shield works without this package. Endpoint telemetry, file integrity,
 journal and auditd ingestion, device discovery, correlation, the evidence
 graph, incident reports, guided Q&A and the response workflow are all
 unaffected. Installing it adds ARP/DHCP/NDP observation, TCP connection
 visibility used by port-scan detection, and outbound DNS observation.
